          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"text\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"text\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "DOCUMENT_PROCESSOR"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1763628919517",
            "name": "parseCourtOrderDocument"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1761625661232"
          },
          "code": "PARSECOURTORDERDOCUMENT",
          "id": "1760692047334",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760692047335_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a medical support notice document parsing expert. Extract information from medical support documents.\n\nDOCUMENT TYPE DETECTION:\n- If contains \"NATIONAL MEDICAL SUPPORT NOTICE\" → Type: \"QMCSO\" (extract PAGES 1-2 ONLY)\n- If contains \"QUALIFIED MEDICAL CHILD SUPPORT ORDER\" or \"QMCSO\" → Type: \"QMCSO\"\n- If contains \"Qualified Domestic Relations Order\" or \"QDRO\" → Type: \"QDRO\"\n- If state court order (handwritten/typed) → Type: \"STATE_COURT_ORDER\"\n- If medical support notice → Type: \"MEDICAL_SUPPORT_NOTICE\"\n\n****Constraints****\n\n-Only analyze text strictly between the markers:\n<--BEGIN COURT ORDER TEXT--> ... <--END COURT ORDER TEXT-->\n-Remove OCR hyphenation, and normalize whitespace.\n-Use ISO 8601 (YYYY-MM-DD) for all dates. If the day is missing and month/year are known, set the date to null rather than guessing.\n-If a field is not found or is ambiguous, set it to the JSON null literal (not an empty string).\n-Return only the final JSON object. No extra text.\n\n****CRITICAL FOR NMSN: READ PAGES 1-2 ONLY - IGNORE PAGES 3-5***\n\n****EXTRACTION RULES****\n- Extract ONLY information present in document\n- Use null for blank/missing fields\n- IGNORE ALL CHECKBOXES - do not read checkbox status\n- For coverage types: extract ONLY Medical, Dental, Vision from document text/tables\n- For handwritten text: extract best-effort interpretation\n- Preserve exact formatting for dates, phone, SSNs\n- Include ALL children/dependents listed\n- If field appears twice: use most complete version\n- Standardize dates to ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD)\n- CREATE SEPARATE DEPENDENT ENTRY FOR EACH COVERAGE TYPE\n- If a dependent has multiple coverages (e.g., Medical + Dental), create duplicate entries with different coverage values\n\n-CourtOrderIdentifier: capture values labeled as Order Identifier., Case No., Cause No., Docket No., Court Order No.,File No.; strip surrounding punctuation/spaces.\n-OrderIssueDate: prefer labels \"Date Issued,\",\"Order Date,\" \"Signed on,\" \"Date of Order.\" Do not use filing date unless explicitly stated as the order date.\n-OrderStartDate: prefer labels \"Date Issued,\",\"Order Date,\" \"Date of Order.\" Do not use filing date unless explicitly stated as the order date.; otherwise null.\n-AgencyName: prefer labels Issuing Agency, Agency name\n-CourtAddress: find the address associated with the court header or signature block; split into AddressLine1, City, State, PostalCode, Country. \n-Participant: the plan participant/employee/parent responsible for employer-sponsored benefits. Use nearby labels: Participant, Employee, Parent, Obligor.\n-CourtOrderDependents: children/spouse/stepchildren listed for medical support.\n-CoverageTypes: capture values labeled Coverage type., Coverage name, Coverage\n-If multiple CoverageTypes are present for a single dependent (e.g., \"Medical, Dental\"), output a separate dependent object for each CoverageType, repeating the DisplayName as needed\n-Only include coverage types explicitly present for a dependent; do not default to any allowed value. If none specified, set CoverageType to Medical, Dental, Vision from document text.\n-DocumentType: prefer labels \"Qualified Medical Child Support Order,\" \"QMCSO,\",\"Qualified Domestic Relations Order,\" \"QDRO\"\n\n****Input****\n<--BEGIN COURT ORDER TEXT-->\n{{$context.$nodes.FETCHCOURTORDERDOCUMENT.$output.text}}\n<--END COURT ORDER TEXT-->\n\nOutput JSON schema (use null for missing values)\n{\n  \"CourtOrderIdentifier\": null,\n  \"OrderStartDate\": null,\n  \"IssuingCourt\": null,\n  \"OrderIssueDate\": null,\n  \"AgencyName\": null,\n  \"DocumentType\": null,\n  \"CourtAddress\": {\n    \"AddressLine1\": null,\n    \"City\": null,\n    \"State\": null,\n    \"PostalCode\": null,\n    \"Country\": null\n  },\n  \"Employee\": {\n    \"DisplayName\": null\n  },\n  \"CourtOrderDependents\": [\n    {\n      \"DisplayName\": \"string\",\n      \"Gender\": \"M | F | null\",\n      \"DateOfBirth\": \"string (YYYY-MM-DD) or null\",\n      \"SSN\": \"string or null\",\n      \"CoverageType\": \"medical | dental | vision\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n  \n\n****CRITICAL RULES*****\nReturn ONLY valid JSON - no markdown, no explanations\n-Use null for missing/blank fields\n-FOR NMSN: Extract pages 1-2 ONLY - ignore pages 3-5\n-IGNORE ALL CHECKBOXES - do not read checkbox status\n-Coverage types: ONLY medical, dental, vision (lowercase)\n-CREATE SEPARATE DEPENDENT ENTRY FOR EACH COVERAGE TYPE\n-If dependent has Medical + Dental: create 2 entries with same name/DOB/SSN but different coverage values\n-Preserve exact SSN, phone, date formats\n\n****Output format****\n{\n  \"CourtOrderIdentifier\": null,\n  \"OrderStartDate\": null,\n  \"IssuingCourt\": null,\n  \"OrderIssueDate\": null,\n  \"AgencyName\":null\n  \"DocumentType\": null,\n  \"CourtAddress\": {\n    \"AddressLine1\": null,\n    \"City\": null,\n    \"State\": null,\n    \"PostalCode\": null,\n    \"Country\": null\n  },\n  \"Employee\": {\n    \"DisplayName\": null\n  },\n  \"CourtOrderDependents\": [\n    {\n      \"DisplayName\": \"Henry Brightleaf\",\n      \"Gender\": \"M\",\n      \"DateOfBirth\": \"2017-11-01\",\n      \"SSN\": null,\n      \"CoverageType\": \"medical\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"DisplayName\": \"Emma Brightleaf\",\n      \"Gender\": \"F\",\n      \"DateOfBirth\": \"2019-02-14\",\n      \"SSN\": null,\n      \"CoverageType\": \"medical\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"DisplayName\": \"Emma Brightleaf\",\n      \"Gender\": \"F\",\n      \"DateOfBirth\": \"2019-02-14\",\n      \"SSN\": null,\n      \"CoverageType\": \"dental\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"Court Order Document Schema\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"State\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"CourtOrderIdentifier\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"OrderStartDate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"IssuingCourt\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"AgencyName\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"DocumentType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"CourtOrderDependents\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"DisplayName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"Gender\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"CoverageType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"DateOfBirth\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"SSN\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"Employee\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"DisplayName\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"CourtAddress\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"City\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"AddressLine1\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Country\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"PostalCode\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
