          "code": "FINDMATCHINGPLANTYPEID",
          "id": "1760692571787",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760692571788_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given two JSON arrays:\n\nplanTypes = {{$context.$variables.planTypeList}}\ncoverageTypes = {{$context.$nodes.MATCHDEPENDENTNAME.$output.matchedDependent}} \n\n### Step 1: Parse and Normalize\n- Extract from each item in planTypes:\n  - Name\n  - PlanTypeId\n- Normalize all plan type names by:\n  - Lowercasing\n  - Trimming whitespace\n  - Removing punctuation and extra symbols\n- Do the same normalization for each 'CoverageTypeName' in coverageTypes.\n\n### Step 2: Matching Logic\nFor each item in 'coverageTypes':\n\n1. **Exact Match**  \n   - If the normalized 'CoverageTypeName' exactly matches a normalized 'planTypes.Name', select that plan.  \n   - Set 'MatchType = \"exact\"'.\n\n2. **Fuzzy / Best Match**  \n   - If no exact match exists, find the 'planTypes' entry whose Name is most semantically or textually similar to the 'CoverageTypeName'.  \n   - Prioritize terms that include or closely resemble these keywords:\n     - medical, health, dental, vision, pharmacy, prescription, behavioral, wellness  \n   - Set 'MatchType = \"fuzzy\"' if a close match is found.\n\n3. **Fallback Match**  \n   - If still no suitable match is found, select **any planType** whose Name contains one of the fallback keywords:\n     - medical, health, dental, or vision  \n   - Choose the first or most relevant of these.\n   - Set 'MatchType = \"fallback\"'.\n\n4. **No Match**  \n   - If absolutely no planTypes contain those keywords, set fields to null and 'MatchType = \"none\"'.\n\n### Step 3: Output Format\nReturn a JSON array like this:\n[\n  {\n    \"CoverageTypeName\": \"<original CoverageTypeName>\",\n    \"MatchedPlanTypeName\": \"<best matched planTypes.Name or fallback>\",\n    \"PlanTypeId\": \"<corresponding PlanTypeId or null>\",\n    \"MatchType\": \"<'exact' | 'fuzzy' | 'fallback' | 'none'>\"\n  },\n  ...\n]\n\nReturn **only valid JSON**, with no extra explanation or text."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema \",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"matchedPlanType\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"CoverageTypeName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"MatchedPlanTypeName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"PlanTypeId\": {\n            \"type\": \"Number\"\n          },\n          \"MatchType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
